#!/bin/sh
# Run on the handheld by the development host over its SSH session, once
# grimoire-host-relay is waiting: join this session's stdio to that Grimoire's
# agent connection. Returns when that Grimoire exits; exits 75 if none waits.
dir=/run/grimoire-agent
relay=$(cat "$dir/waiting" 2>/dev/null)
rm -f "$dir/waiting"
if [ -z "$relay" ] || ! kill -0 "$relay" 2>/dev/null; then
  echo "No Grimoire is waiting for an agent." >&2
  exit 75
fi
# Background commands read /dev/null unless stdin is given explicitly.
cat <&0 >"$dir/from-host" &
feeder=$!
cat <"$dir/to-host"
kill "$feeder" 2>/dev/null
exit 0
